.TH "COMPLYCTL\-PROVIDER\-AMPEL" "1" "September 2026" "ComplyTime Manual"
.SH NAME
complyctl\-provider\-ampel \- Ampel scanning provider for complyctl
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]complyctl\-provider\-ampel\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]complyctl\-provider\-ampel\f[R] is a gRPC plugin for
\f[B]complyctl\f[R](1) that provides compliance scanning capabilities
using the Ampel evaluation engine.
It is not invoked directly by users; \f[B]complyctl\f[R] discovers and
launches it automatically when the provider is installed.
.PP
The provider receives assessment configurations from \f[B]complyctl\f[R]
and evaluates repository configurations against granular security
policies (e.g., branch protection rules) using the \f[B]snappy\f[R] and
\f[B]ampel\f[R] CLI tools.
Results include per\-tenet messages and remediation guidance.
.PP
Communication with \f[B]complyctl\f[R] uses the hashicorp/go\-plugin
gRPC interface, implementing three RPCs: \f[B]Describe\f[R],
\f[B]Generate\f[R], and \f[B]Scan\f[R].
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is provided through variables defined in assessment plan
targets.
These variables are passed to the provider via \f[B]complyctl\f[R] and
are not set manually by the user.
.TP
\f[B]url\f[R] (required)
HTTPS URL of the repository to scan.
Must use the HTTPS scheme.
Example: \f[B]https://github.com/org/repo\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]specs\f[R] (required)
Comma\-separated list of spec references identifying the policy files to
evaluate.
Example: \f[B]builtin:github/branch\-rules.yaml\f[R].
Path traversal sequences (\f[B]../\f[R]) are rejected.
.TP
\f[B]branches\f[R] (optional)
Comma\-separated list of branches to scan.
Must match the pattern \f[B][a\-zA\-Z0\-9._/\-]+\f[R].
Path traversal sequences are rejected.
Default: \f[B]main\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]access_token\f[R] (optional)
Authentication token for accessing private repositories.
Rejected if it contains newlines or null bytes.
.TP
\f[B]platform\f[R] (optional)
Platform hint for self\-hosted instances (e.g., \f[B]github\f[R],
\f[B]gitlab\f[R]).
Used when hostname\-based detection fails to identify the platform.
Default: auto\-detected from the URL hostname.
.TP
\f[B]ampel_policy_dir\f[R] (optional, global variable)
Custom directory containing granular Ampel policy source files.
Takes second priority after complypack content.
Default: \f[B].complytime/ampel/granular\-policies/\f[R]
.SH ENVIRONMENT
No environment variables are read directly by this provider.
.SH EXTERNAL TOOLS
Requires \f[B]snappy\f[R] and \f[B]ampel\f[R] CLI tools at runtime.
These tools are not currently packaged in Fedora and must be installed
separately.
See the Carabiner project for installation instructions: \c
.UR https://github.com/carabiner-dev
.UE \c
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]\(ti/.local/share/complytime/ampel/\f[R]
Provider workspace directory for scan configuration and policy files.
.SH EXIT CODES
This provider is a gRPC subprocess managed by \f[B]complyctl\f[R].
Exit codes follow the hashicorp/go\-plugin protocol and are not
user\-facing.
